      "headerNotes": [],
      "steps": [
        {
          "kind": "tip",
          "title": "Identifying Serbia",
          "items": [
            {
              "kind": "centeredImage",
              "id": "zDx3",
              "imageUrl": "/images/serbia/transparent-RS_Summary.png"
            },
            {
              "kind": "tip",
              "id": "qGEx",
              "data": {
                "image": {
                  "imageUrl": "/images/serbia/bollard.png",
                  "imageLink": "https://goo.gl/maps/HHzC7GHNbsHNodDm8",
                  "alt": "",
                  "width": 0.5
                },
                "text": [
                  "Serbia has a few bollard designs, however most of them will have an **off-centred reflector.** The bollards are usually flat, with no depth to them."
                ]
              },
              "tags": [
                "bollard"
              ]
            },
            {
              "kind": "tip",
              "id": "VSVy",
              "data": {
                "image": {
                  "imageUrl": "/images/serbia/Screenshot_2023-07-01_160306.png",
                  "imageLink": "https://goo.gl/maps/Yc1Lbv5frL5g4kx17",
                  "alt": "",
                  "width": 0.5
                },
                "text": [
                  "Serbia uses **B-Profile** guardrails exclusively.",
                  "NOTE: North Macedonia does not use B-Profile guardrails. For a good overview of European guardrails, see [this infographic](/images/serbia/europeguardrail.png)."
                ]
              },
              "tags": [
                "guardrail"
              ]
            },
            {
              "kind": "tip",
              "id": "WqwF",
              "data": {
                "image": {
                  "imageUrl": "/images/serbia/Screenshot_2023-07-01_160357.png",
                  "imageLink": "https://goo.gl/maps/dSYX1E85L6sAcwwG9",
                  "alt": "",
                  "width": 0.5
                },
                "text": [
                  "Serbia uses chevrons with a **black arrow** on a **white** background.",
                  "NOTE: Within Europe, these chevrons can also be found in Slovenia, Montenegro and North Macedonia."
                ]
              },
              "tags": [
                "chevron/sign"
              ]
            },
            {
              "kind": "tip",
              "id": "eWgo",
              "data": {
                "image": {
                  "imageUrl": "/images/serbia/Serbia_Plate.png",
                  "imageLink": "/images/serbia/Serbia_Plate.png",
                  "alt": "",
                  "width": 0.5
                },
                "text": [
                  "Serbian licence plates are white with a **blue strip** on the left. Agricultural plates, on vehicles such as tractors, are **green**.",
                  "NOTE: Croatian and North Macedonian plates typically do not have a blue strip."
                ]
              },
              "tags": [
                "license plates"
              ]
            },
            {
              "kind": "tip",
              "id": "6jty",
              "data": {
                "image": {
                  "imageUrl": "/images/serbia/rs_cyrillic_fixed.png",
                  "imageLink": "/images/serbia/rs_language.png",
                  "alt": "",
                  "width": 0.5
                },
                "text": [
                  "Serbian is a Slavic language which uses both the **Cyrillic** and Latin script. These letters are unique to Serbian:",
                  "- Ђ ђ",
                  "- Ћ ћ",
                  "These letters are found in Serbian and Macedonian:",
                  "- Љ љ",
                  "- Њ њ",
                  "- Џ џ"
                ]
              },
              "tags": [
                "language"
              ]
            },
            {
              "kind": "tip",
              "id": "C8Jw",
              "data": {
                "image": {
                  "imageUrl": "/images/serbia/rs_languagelatin.png",
                  "imageLink": "/images/serbia/rs_languagelatin.png",
                  "alt": "",
                  "width": 0.5
                },
                "text": [
                  "When written in the **Latin** script, Serbian uses the special letters Č, Ć, Đ, Š and Ž. Note that all of these letters may also be found in Croatian and Montenegrin."
                ]
              },
              "tags": [
                "language"
              ]
            },
            {
              "kind": "tip",
              "id": "SDu4",
              "data": {
                "image": {
                  "imageUrl": "/images/serbia/Truck Serbia.png",
                  "imageLink": "https://maps.app.goo.gl/sWnSBLcjgBGRNiD37",
                  "alt": "",
                  "width": 0.5
                },
                "text": [
                  "Serbia has **4 different truck colours** that were used in different areas."
                ]
              },
              "tags": [
                "important",
                "coverage"
              ]
            },
            {
              "kind": "tip",
              "id": "V8kh",
              "data": {
                "image": {
                  "imageUrl": "/images/serbia/Smallcam Serbia.png",
                  "imageLink": "https://maps.app.goo.gl/eX2AP5vfj7sT2i4e8",
                  "alt": "",
                  "width": 0.5
                },
                "text": [
                  "Serbia also has Generation 4 “smallcam” coverage, which is mounted lower than regular Generation 4 and has a relatively big circular blur with a small protrusion at the front. The blur can also be fully transparent, making it harder to spot. And a short antenna or black blur can be seen on the backside.",
                  "NOTE: Most of the Balkans also have Smallcam."
                ]
              },
              "tags": [
                "coverage"
              ]
            },
            {
              "kind": "tip",
              "id": "LpbY",
              "data": {
                "image": {
                  "imageUrl": "/images/serbia/image.png",
                  "imageLink": "https://goo.gl/maps/hCMFwfkEBsVpPVss9",
                  "alt": "",
                  "width": 0.5
                },
                "text": [
                  "Most of the generation 3 coverage in Serbia was taken by a Google car with **no antenna**.",
                  "NOTE: Other than North Macedonia, almost all of central and eastern Europe has antenna coverage in Generation 3."
                ]
              },
              "tags": [
                "coverage"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "tip",
          "title": "Regional/district-specific clues",
          "items": [
            {
              "kind": "tip",
              "id": "mTBk",
              "data": {
                "image": {
                  "imageUrl": "/images/serbia/Serbia_Coverage_Map_.png",
                  "imageLink": "/images/serbia/Serbia_Coverage_Map_.png",
                  "alt": "",
                  "width": 0.5
                },
                "text": [
                  "This is a generation 3 coverage map of Serbia. Most of the coverage is in the north in Vojvodina, around Belgrade and in the southeast around Niš. Kosovo does not have any coverage."
                ]
              },
              "tags": [
                "coverage"
              ]
            },
            {
              "kind": "tip",
              "id": "VetX",
              "data": {
                "image": {
                  "imageUrl": "/images/serbia/rl3c_rs_serbia_map_illdtmcolgw30s_ja_hres.jpg",
                  "imageLink": "/images/serbia/rl3c_rs_serbia_map_illdtmcolgw30s_ja_hres.jpg",
                  "alt": "",
                  "width": 0.5
                },
                "text": [
                  "In the north of Serbia in the Vojvodina region, from the Hungarian border to Belgrade, the landscape is **extremely flat**, with no hills whatsoever. A slight ridge however can be seen at Fruška Gora National Park.",
                  "A more hilly landscape can be seen in the central-southern region. The most mountainous regions of Serbia are found in the southwest and southeast, where the Dinaric Alps, Carpathian and Balkan mountains run through Serbia."
                ]
              },
              "tags": [
                "landscape"
              ]
            },
            {
              "kind": "tip",
              "id": "w6kX",
              "data": {
                "image": {
                  "imageUrl": "/images/serbia/area_codes_colourized.png",
                  "imageLink": "/images/serbia/area_codes_colourized.png",
                  "alt": "",
                  "width": 0.5
                },
                "text": [
                  "Serbia uses 2 digit area codes, with the first digit **between 1 and 3**. Area codes starting with 2 are found in the north, area codes starting with 1 are found in central and eastern Serbia. Area codes starting with 3 are found in the south-west."
                ]
              },
              "tags": [
                "moving info"
              ]
            },
            {
              "kind": "tip",
              "id": "un4M",
              "data": {
                "image": {
                  "imageUrl": "/images/serbia/vojvodina.png",
                  "imageLink": "https://goo.gl/maps/HJB7gpLKUKhP7cQT7",
                  "alt": "",
                  "width": 0.573
                },
                "text": [
                  "Vojvodina, the northern region between the Hungarian border and Belgrade, can be recognized by the **flat**, **agricultural landscape**. The landscape will be completely flat with **no hills whatsoever**."
                ]
              },
              "tags": [
                "landscape"
              ]
            },
            {
              "kind": "tip",
              "id": "kehq",
              "data": {
                "image": {
                  "imageUrl": "/images/serbia/ridge.png",
                  "imageLink": "https://goo.gl/maps/5wYfyg65fHuNuj949",
                  "alt": "",
                  "width": 0.573
                },
                "text": [
                  "This slight **ridge** in an otherwise flat landscape can be seen in Fruška Gora National Park, southwest of Novi Sad."
                ]
              },
              "tags": [
                "landscape"
              ]
            },
            {
              "kind": "tip",
              "id": "enVL",
              "data": {
                "image": {
                  "imageUrl": "/images/serbia/rolling.png",
                  "imageLink": "https://goo.gl/maps/HYWXp5ijqEucbFTz7",
                  "alt": "",
                  "width": 0.573
                },
                "text": [
                  "Central-northern Serbia can be recognized by the **slight rolling hills**."
                ]
              },
              "tags": [
                "landscape"
              ]
            },
            {
              "kind": "tip",
              "id": "QMqw",
              "data": {
                "image": {
                  "imageUrl": "/images/serbia/basin.png",
                  "imageLink": "https://goo.gl/maps/J4e94gw7DFAin1Ee8",
                  "alt": "",
                  "width": 0.573
                },
                "text": [
                  "A similarly rolling landscape can be seen in the southern Morava River basin, however **larger hills and mountains** can be seen."
                ]
              },
              "tags": [
                "landscape"
              ]
            },
            {
              "kind": "tip",
              "id": "RnNO",
              "data": {
                "image": {
                  "imageUrl": "/images/serbia/mountain.png",
                  "imageLink": "https://goo.gl/maps/dgS7WSfnGZtK9cvx6",
                  "alt": "",
                  "width": 0.573
                },
                "text": [
                  "A **lush**, **green**, **mountainous** landscape can be seen in the south and southeast, along the Bulgarian and Kosovo border."
                ]
              },
              "tags": [
                "landscape"
              ]
            },
            {
              "kind": "tip",
              "id": "WCh2",
              "data": {
                "image": {
                  "imageUrl": "/images/serbia/fall.png",
                  "imageLink": "https://goo.gl/maps/BssvgC1pp83KmsWS7",
                  "alt": "",
                  "width": 0.573
                },
                "text": [
                  "Generation 3 **Fall coverage** can be seen in this region south of Čačak, and a small area around Valjevo."
                ]
              },
              "tags": [
                "coverage",
                "landscape"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "tip",
          "title": "Spotlight",
          "items": [
            {
              "kind": "tip",
              "id": "8vGG",
              "data": {
                "image": {
                  "imageUrl": "/images/serbia/rs_antenna.png",
                  "imageLink": "https://goo.gl/maps/dQpeAgnPjEJHoG348",
                  "alt": "",
                  "width": 0.573
                },
                "text": [
                  "A white Google Car with a **short antenna** can be seen in Novi Sad, Kovilj, in and around Belgrade, Niš, and the E75 connecting them.",
                  "NOTE: The white car is not always visible."
                ]
              },
              "tags": [
                "coverage"
              ]
            },
            {
              "kind": "tip",
              "id": "yQCt",
              "data": {
                "image": {
                  "imageUrl": "/images/serbia/vrsac_mountains.png",
                  "imageLink": "https://goo.gl/maps/74se7bmpkSF8wF966",
                  "alt": "",
                  "width": 0.573
                },
                "text": [
                  "The distinct **Vršac Mountains** can be seen east of Vršac near the Romanian border. The mountains protrude out from a flat landscape and [vineyards](https://goo.gl/maps/e2hLdz6HJw4kWN778) can commonly be seen to the south of the mountains. The [Vršac Castle](https://goo.gl/maps/WzaCRBL14QdDEdre7) can also be seen atop the mountain."
                ]
              },
              "tags": [
                "landscape"
              ]
            },
            {
              "kind": "tip",
              "id": "ajNO",
              "data": {
                "image": {
                  "imageUrl": "/images/serbia/hungarian.png",
                  "imageLink": "https://goo.gl/maps/LMC1Ro9E71Eyz2wg8",
                  "alt": "",
                  "width": 0.573
                },
                "text": [
                  "**Bilingual signs** with Serbian alongside Hungarian can be seen in northern Vojvodina, where there is a Hungarian majority."
                ]
              },
              "tags": [
                "language"
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "draftChangelog": []
    },
    "communityDocs": []
  }
}